---
title: Flexplot - Graphically Based Data Analysis
name: flexplot
version: 0.7.2
jms: '1.0'
authors:
  - Dustin Fife
maintainer: Dustin Fife <fife.dustin@gmail.com>
date: '2019-08-05'
type: R
description: >-
  The flexplot suite is a graphically-based set of tools for doing data
  analysis. Flexplot allows users to specify a formula and the software
  automatically choses what sort of graphic to present. glinmod allows linear
  modeling and, like flexplot,  chooses an appropriate graphic to present
  alongside the statistical 
analyses:
  - title: General Linear Model
    name: glmbasic
    ns: flexplot
    menuGroup: Flexplot
    menuTitle: General Linear Model
    options:
      - name: data
        type: Data
      - name: out
        title: Dependent variable
        type: Variable
      - name: preds
        title: Predictor variable
        type: Variables
      - name: graphic
        title: Analysis graphs
        type: Bool
        default: true
      - name: graphicassump
        title: Diagnostics
        type: Bool
        default: false
      - name: estimates
        title: Estimates and effect eizes
        type: Bool
        default: true
      - name: se
        title: Standard errors
        type: Bool
        default: true
      - name: line
        title: Fitted line (for scatterplots)
        type: List
        options:
          - Loess
          - Regression
          - Logistic
        default: Loess
      - name: center
        title: Center/spread (for dot plots)
        type: List
        options:
          - Median + quartiles
          - Mean + sterr
          - Mean + stdev
        default: Median + quartiles
